1
00:01:27,017 --> 00:01:30,654
Vote for Ruam Thai Chana.
No. 2 on the ballot.

2
00:01:30,654 --> 00:01:34,054
Trust me, you'll be rich.

3
00:01:38,954 --> 00:01:40,646
Please vote for Ruam Thai Chana.

4
00:01:40,646 --> 00:01:44,630
Vote for Ruam Thai Chana. Thank you.

5
00:01:44,630 --> 00:01:46,734
Don't forget to vote for us.

6
00:01:54,382 --> 00:01:57,574
- Hello, Weechana.
- Can I take a picture with you?

7
00:02:02,758 --> 00:02:04,559
Vote No. 2.

8
00:02:06,614 --> 00:02:07,634
[Domino]

9
00:02:07,634 --> 00:02:09,635
Thank you. Vote for Ruam Thai Chana.

10
00:02:09,635 --> 00:02:11,382
Cast your vote for No. 2.

11
00:02:11,382 --> 00:02:16,254
<i>Sorry, the number you have dialed
is currently unavailable.</i>

12
00:02:17,241 --> 00:02:19,785
Mark your ballot for No. 2.

13
00:02:19,785 --> 00:02:21,894
- Can I get a selfie with you?
- Sure.

14
00:02:21,894 --> 00:02:25,054
The food looks amazing.

15
00:02:26,446 --> 00:02:29,870
- There you go.
- Enjoy your meal.

16
00:02:29,870 --> 00:02:32,034
- You have to wake up early, don't you?
- Yes.

17
00:02:32,034 --> 00:02:34,425
I'm a regular customer,
so you remember me, right?

18
00:02:34,425 --> 00:02:35,934
Yeah.

19
00:02:35,934 --> 00:02:38,035
Hello, please vote for us.

20
00:02:38,035 --> 00:02:41,054
- Don't forget to vote for us.
- You look even better in person.

21
00:02:44,217 --> 00:02:46,521
There was a lunch break in the schedule,

22
00:02:46,521 --> 00:02:49,134
so I thought we'd eat at Aunt Da's place.

23
00:02:49,134 --> 00:02:52,094
You'll get to see your aunt too.
Isn't that nice?

24
00:02:52,814 --> 00:02:54,801
Yeah.

25
00:02:54,801 --> 00:02:57,494
Aunt Da, hello.

26
00:02:57,494 --> 00:03:00,561
- Hello, Mr. Weechana.
- Hello.

27
00:03:00,561 --> 00:03:04,734
You don't have to be so formal.
We're all friends here.

28
00:03:05,734 --> 00:03:07,920
Which one would you recommend?

29
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:11,193
- All of them.
- They all look good.

30
00:03:11,193 --> 00:03:15,540
I'm a regular here. The food is excellent.

31
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:18,473
Welcome! Please enjoy.

32
00:03:19,518 --> 00:03:21,156
Eva.

33
00:03:21,156 --> 00:03:24,094
Eat up, dear. You've gotten so thin.

34
00:03:26,964 --> 00:03:28,765
Are you tired?

35
00:03:29,721 --> 00:03:31,284
I'm about to pass out.

36
00:03:31,284 --> 00:03:34,654
They've been bossing me around
since this morning. My head's spinning.

37
00:03:39,190 --> 00:03:42,934
Hey, Weechana, Eva!
Let's take a selfie together.

38
00:03:42,934 --> 00:03:44,814
- Okay, sure.
- Let's take a picture.

39
00:03:46,070 --> 00:03:48,017
Weechana, you go first.

40
00:03:48,017 --> 00:03:50,513
Aunt Da, let's take a selfie together.

41
00:03:50,513 --> 00:03:52,894
Say cheese!

42
00:03:55,921 --> 00:03:58,145
Can you hold this one?

43
00:03:58,145 --> 00:03:59,937
This one, hold this one.

44
00:03:59,937 --> 00:04:01,852
Yeah, hold this one.

45
00:04:01,852 --> 00:04:02,980
That's right.

46
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:07,214
And smile like your business
is booming today!

47
00:04:07,214 --> 00:04:09,806
Bigger smile, Auntie.

48
00:04:09,806 --> 00:04:12,494
One more. Keep smiling.

49
00:04:12,494 --> 00:04:16,574
That's enough, Pie. Give her a break.

50
00:04:16,574 --> 00:04:18,974
It's just for appearances.

51
00:04:20,076 --> 00:04:21,670
I'm not taking her anywhere.

52
00:04:21,670 --> 00:04:24,334
And she's not my standard.

53
00:04:25,204 --> 00:04:26,734
Do you understand it?

54
00:04:26,734 --> 00:04:32,774
Well, high standards are
no excuse for bad manners.

55
00:04:35,913 --> 00:04:37,714
Am I right, Weechana?

56
00:04:38,412 --> 00:04:39,779
Yes.

57
00:04:41,342 --> 00:04:43,321
Should I translate it too,

58
00:04:43,321 --> 00:04:45,822
in case your Thai isn't that good?

59
00:04:45,822 --> 00:04:50,434
Having high standards is
no excuse for bad manners.

60
00:04:52,814 --> 00:04:54,388
Let's go, Auntie.

61
00:04:54,388 --> 00:04:56,189
Take a nap.

62
00:04:58,634 --> 00:05:00,079
Okay.

63
00:05:07,670 --> 00:05:10,481
Hang in there, Auntie. Just a bit more.

64
00:05:10,481 --> 00:05:12,577
They will leave soon.

65
00:05:12,577 --> 00:05:14,129
I'm totally fine.

66
00:05:14,129 --> 00:05:16,814
The Kathin festival was
way more exhausting than this.

67
00:05:17,548 --> 00:05:21,374
What's your deal?
I thought you already broke up with him.

68
00:05:23,982 --> 00:05:25,860
We did break up.

69
00:05:25,860 --> 00:05:30,681
But he asked me to stay
and help with his campaign first.

70
00:05:30,681 --> 00:05:32,534
It's over between us now.

71
00:05:36,974 --> 00:05:39,172
Auntie, listen.

72
00:05:39,172 --> 00:05:43,482
If Weechana asks you
to go somewhere with him, don't go.

73
00:05:43,482 --> 00:05:46,485
No matter what he says,
even if he brings up my name,

74
00:05:46,485 --> 00:05:49,292
don't go with him. Got it?

75
00:05:49,292 --> 00:05:51,708
Yeah, I got it.

76
00:05:51,708 --> 00:05:55,174
I've been watching him.
I don't think he is a good guy.

77
00:05:55,801 --> 00:05:59,094
Eva, you need to be careful.

78
00:05:59,758 --> 00:06:02,374
How come Domino isn't with you?

79
00:06:03,305 --> 00:06:06,414
I haven't been able to reach her at all.
I have no idea where she went.

80
00:06:06,414 --> 00:06:08,574
She's not answering my calls
or replying to my texts.

81
00:06:08,574 --> 00:06:11,214
I'm thinking about
sending someone to look for her.

82
00:06:21,054 --> 00:06:22,617
<i>I can't reach Domino.</i>

83
00:06:22,617 --> 00:06:26,254
<i>If you're not busy,
could you check on her at my place for me?</i>

84
00:06:28,034 --> 00:06:30,894
<i>Sure. I'll keep you posted.</i>

85
00:06:30,894 --> 00:06:34,534
<i>And send me your location too, just in case.</i>

86
00:06:42,614 --> 00:06:44,094
Boat.

87
00:06:44,094 --> 00:06:45,595
Eva just texted me.

88
00:06:45,595 --> 00:06:47,560
She hasn't been able to reach Domino
since they split up this morning.

89
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,548
- What?
- Yeah.

90
00:06:48,548 --> 00:06:51,494
Go check on Domino at Eva's place.
I'll rush over to see Eva.

91
00:06:53,102 --> 00:06:54,702
Domino is missing.

92
00:06:54,702 --> 00:06:56,756
So why aren't we out there looking for her?

93
00:06:56,756 --> 00:06:58,862
Why are you rushing to Eva instead?

94
00:06:58,862 --> 00:07:02,110
If Domino's gone,
who's going to be there for Eva?

95
00:07:02,110 --> 00:07:03,374
I see.

96
00:07:03,374 --> 00:07:06,212
Just go. Keep me posted, okay?

97
00:07:06,212 --> 00:07:08,014
Please be careful.

98
00:07:10,836 --> 00:07:13,374
You too, buddy.

99
00:07:16,142 --> 00:07:19,494
Thank you so much, Aunt Da.
The food was absolutely delicious.

100
00:07:20,934 --> 00:07:23,441
Are you sure?

101
00:07:23,441 --> 00:07:25,494
You barely touched your food.

102
00:07:26,326 --> 00:07:28,481
Yeah, the food was good.

103
00:07:28,481 --> 00:07:30,577
I actually have to get going.

104
00:07:30,577 --> 00:07:33,710
I'll bring Eva back to see you another time.

105
00:07:33,710 --> 00:07:35,401
Eva is my niece.

106
00:07:35,401 --> 00:07:38,894
She doesn't have to wait for you.
She's welcome here anytime.

107
00:07:39,508 --> 00:07:41,214
Come visit me more often, okay?

108
00:07:41,214 --> 00:07:43,015
Okay.

109
00:07:50,774 --> 00:07:53,094
Oh my God!

110
00:07:54,254 --> 00:07:56,774
This should be fun.

111
00:08:01,316 --> 00:08:03,134
- Hello.
- Hello.

112
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:08,061
Why is he here?

113
00:08:08,061 --> 00:08:10,396
I asked him to come.

114
00:08:10,396 --> 00:08:12,124
Yeah, exactly.

115
00:08:12,124 --> 00:08:13,686
Why did you ask him to come?

116
00:08:13,686 --> 00:08:16,814
I couldn't reach Domino,
so I asked him to fill in for her.

117
00:08:16,814 --> 00:08:19,580
Right, I see.

118
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:21,694
Can you be a manager too?

119
00:08:23,310 --> 00:08:25,556
Come on, I really don't have a choice.

120
00:08:25,556 --> 00:08:28,756
I couldn't reach her,
and that's not like her at all.

121
00:08:28,756 --> 00:08:31,348
You have no idea where she is, right?

122
00:08:31,348 --> 00:08:33,699
How am I supposed to know?

123
00:08:33,699 --> 00:08:36,574
I'll ask Pat to look for her.

124
00:08:38,158 --> 00:08:39,838
Boat's at the condo now.

125
00:08:39,838 --> 00:08:42,980
I'll keep you posted.
You can get back to campaigning.

126
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:45,217
I'll stay nearby in case you need me.

127
00:08:45,217 --> 00:08:46,716
You can wait for me here.

128
00:08:46,716 --> 00:08:49,294
Once I'm done here,
we'll go look for Domino together.

129
00:08:49,294 --> 00:08:50,727
Sure.

130
00:08:51,996 --> 00:08:53,797
Can you reach Pat?

131
00:08:59,582 --> 00:09:01,157
Let's go.

132
00:09:16,997 --> 00:09:20,471
Auntie, this is Pun.

133
00:09:21,334 --> 00:09:24,334
He is... my friend.

134
00:09:27,713 --> 00:09:30,945
I see. He's your friend.

135
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:33,614
Go. Hurry up and get it over with.

136
00:09:43,286 --> 00:09:46,033
Vote for Ruam Thai Chana. Vote No. 2.

137
00:09:46,033 --> 00:09:49,320
<i>This campaign trail has shown me</i>

138
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:52,479
- Vote for us.
- <i>just how much hardship...</i>

139
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:54,399
<i>people are facing every day.</i>

140
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:57,766
<i>We may not be able
to solve every problem today.</i>

141
00:09:57,766 --> 00:10:02,716
<i>But over the next four years,
we can do it for sure.</i>

142
00:10:02,716 --> 00:10:05,177
<i>I will work to give everyone
a better quality of life,</i>

143
00:10:05,177 --> 00:10:07,422
- <i>better education,</i>
- Vote for Ruam Thai Chana.

144
00:10:07,422 --> 00:10:10,254
<i>And greater financial security.</i>

145
00:10:10,254 --> 00:10:14,297
<i>Because those are the foundations
of a better future for all of us.</i>

146
00:10:14,297 --> 00:10:17,134
Eva, are you a guinea pig?

147
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:22,821
Everything Weechana just talked about,
he's already done for you.

148
00:10:22,821 --> 00:10:25,534
Since when did you become such a good person?

149
00:10:26,585 --> 00:10:28,041
Listen to me.

150
00:10:28,041 --> 00:10:31,582
You don't need an education
to be a good person.

151
00:10:31,582 --> 00:10:34,132
You don't have to be rich, either.

152
00:10:34,132 --> 00:10:38,558
A good person can do good
and succeed anywhere.

153
00:10:38,558 --> 00:10:41,632
I guess no one ever taught you that, Pie.

154
00:10:41,632 --> 00:10:43,854
I understand.

155
00:10:43,854 --> 00:10:45,974
You're getting pretty bold these days.

156
00:10:46,833 --> 00:10:48,657
So what?

157
00:10:48,657 --> 00:10:50,458
You got a problem with that?

158
00:11:05,134 --> 00:11:07,339
[Domino]

159
00:11:11,092 --> 00:11:16,054
<i>Sorry, the number you have dialed
is currently unavailable.</i>

160
00:11:20,923 --> 00:11:22,734
I'm done for the day.

161
00:11:23,550 --> 00:11:26,134
Have you gotten a hold of her yet?
Do you need any help?

162
00:11:26,134 --> 00:11:27,694
No, I haven't.

163
00:11:27,694 --> 00:11:31,341
I'd better get going.
I need to get back and see my aunt.

164
00:11:32,254 --> 00:11:34,958
To see your aunt or to see him?

165
00:11:34,958 --> 00:11:37,961
- What?
- I am standing right here.

166
00:11:37,961 --> 00:11:39,254
I can have my team help you.

167
00:11:39,254 --> 00:11:42,542
Why would you go back to a man
who has nothing to offer?

168
00:11:42,542 --> 00:11:44,585
Because I trust him.

169
00:11:44,585 --> 00:11:48,254
- Eva.
- Weechana, hi.

170
00:11:50,494 --> 00:11:52,142
Would you like a picture with him?

171
00:11:52,142 --> 00:11:54,054
- Oh, thank you.
- Let's get in.

172
00:11:54,054 --> 00:11:57,801
I didn't think I'd make it.
Can I get a picture with you?

173
00:11:57,801 --> 00:11:59,774
I'm so nervous that I'm shaking.

174
00:12:00,473 --> 00:12:03,044
Pat, can you cancel the gym review for me?

175
00:12:03,044 --> 00:12:06,134
I'm exhausted. I just can't go anymore.

176
00:12:14,174 --> 00:12:16,134
Seriously?

177
00:12:16,134 --> 00:12:19,062
You really think I want a new car that bad?

178
00:12:19,062 --> 00:12:20,977
Get in the car first.

179
00:12:20,977 --> 00:12:23,854
I'll tell you what this is all about.

180
00:12:35,734 --> 00:12:37,969
During her school break,

181
00:12:37,969 --> 00:12:42,305
she put on little shows for the customers
every single day.

182
00:12:42,305 --> 00:12:44,636
As for her homework?
She didn't even think about it.

183
00:12:44,636 --> 00:12:48,374
She'd pick flowers,
make herself a flower crown,

184
00:12:48,374 --> 00:12:52,374
then dance around in front of the shop.

185
00:12:53,564 --> 00:12:56,654
But that's what she loves,
so I just let her be.

186
00:12:57,454 --> 00:12:58,714
Hey.

187
00:12:59,684 --> 00:13:01,734
Did you ask him to do the dishes?

188
00:13:02,398 --> 00:13:03,972
No, I offered to help.

189
00:13:03,972 --> 00:13:06,372
I'm really good at this.

190
00:13:06,372 --> 00:13:08,173
It was my first job.

191
00:13:09,417 --> 00:13:11,574
There's still some soap here.

192
00:13:12,868 --> 00:13:14,669
I can see it.

193
00:13:16,446 --> 00:13:19,134
Hey, it's Boat. He's calling.

194
00:13:19,134 --> 00:13:20,694
Go ahead and answer it.

195
00:13:23,870 --> 00:13:26,174
Hi, Boat. It's Eva.

196
00:13:29,896 --> 00:13:31,697
What did you say?

197
00:13:52,364 --> 00:13:53,590
Weechana!

198
00:13:53,590 --> 00:13:55,873
- Eva?
- Domino jumped off the building.

199
00:13:55,873 --> 00:13:57,201
That's impossible.

200
00:13:57,201 --> 00:13:59,617
She only went upstairs to get her car keys
so she could leave with us.

201
00:13:59,617 --> 00:14:02,145
You were the one who made her go upstairs.

202
00:14:02,145 --> 00:14:04,865
You planned everything.

203
00:14:04,865 --> 00:14:06,385
I didn't know anything about this.

204
00:14:06,385 --> 00:14:10,721
Mark my words. If anything happens to her,
I'll expose everything.

205
00:14:10,721 --> 00:14:14,414
I'll tell everyone about every
disgusting thing you've ever done.

206
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:36,574
- Where's the ER?
- To your right.

207
00:14:47,622 --> 00:14:49,169
What?

208
00:14:49,169 --> 00:14:51,190
Why are you here?

209
00:14:51,190 --> 00:14:52,991
You need to leave.

210
00:14:54,932 --> 00:14:56,332
Stop.

211
00:14:58,153 --> 00:15:00,234
What's this?

212
00:15:01,254 --> 00:15:02,558
What?

213
00:15:02,558 --> 00:15:05,166
It won't take long.

214
00:15:05,166 --> 00:15:09,422
Ms. Jit heard you dropped your AirPods.

215
00:15:09,422 --> 00:15:15,934
She wanted to know
whether you and Eva saw anything.

216
00:15:33,580 --> 00:15:37,854
Grandma Jit...
told you to break into Eva's place,

217
00:15:39,217 --> 00:15:42,654
and you showed up with a man
who looked like he was going to attack me.

218
00:15:43,596 --> 00:15:45,397
What is your plan?

219
00:15:52,734 --> 00:15:54,535
What are you doing?

220
00:15:56,265 --> 00:15:58,066
A knife?

221
00:15:59,721 --> 00:16:01,522
I saw something.

222
00:16:04,726 --> 00:16:07,788
I saw Weechana beat up the reporter,

223
00:16:07,788 --> 00:16:09,694
who later died.

224
00:16:10,961 --> 00:16:14,614
Eva didn't see any of it.
She was in the restroom.

225
00:16:15,433 --> 00:16:17,497
I couldn't bring myself to tell her.

226
00:16:17,497 --> 00:16:19,219
He was her boyfriend, after all.

227
00:16:19,219 --> 00:16:21,020
You know what I mean?

228
00:16:25,214 --> 00:16:28,254
Ms. Jit would like you to work for her.

229
00:16:29,420 --> 00:16:32,209
What is your rate?

230
00:16:32,209 --> 00:16:35,041
Work? What do you mean?

231
00:16:37,673 --> 00:16:40,612
Report everything about Eva to her.

232
00:16:40,612 --> 00:16:43,454
Everything on Eva's schedule
has to go through her as well.

233
00:16:47,052 --> 00:16:48,428
500,000.

234
00:16:49,430 --> 00:16:53,334
I get paid really well working for Eva.

235
00:16:54,830 --> 00:16:56,631
No problem.

236
00:16:58,233 --> 00:17:00,057
I'll need the iCloud password.

237
00:17:00,057 --> 00:17:03,334
I want to check what's in the account.

238
00:17:05,113 --> 00:17:06,914
Well...

239
00:17:14,625 --> 00:17:16,126
This one, too.

240
00:17:17,398 --> 00:17:20,014
I don't know Eva's password.

241
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:29,880
You are deleting the videos
of Weechana assaulting people.

242
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:32,319
[Voice recording]
Why are you deleting them?

243
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:45,080
[Voice recording]

244
00:17:53,708 --> 00:17:55,509
Get back here!

245
00:18:00,428 --> 00:18:03,340
Please let me go. Please.

246
00:18:03,340 --> 00:18:05,254
I won't do anything.

247
00:18:07,894 --> 00:18:09,601
Help!

248
00:18:09,601 --> 00:18:12,174
Get back here!

249
00:18:28,369 --> 00:18:30,454
We rushed out of there.

250
00:18:30,454 --> 00:18:33,156
But we've already taken care of
the security camera footage at the condo.

251
00:18:33,156 --> 00:18:36,414
Have all the videos of Weechana been deleted?

252
00:18:37,353 --> 00:18:39,793
We've deleted everything
from Domino's laptop.

253
00:18:39,793 --> 00:18:44,166
We still can't access Eva's
because it's password-protected.

254
00:18:44,166 --> 00:18:45,852
We need to find a hacker to get into it.

255
00:18:45,852 --> 00:18:49,534
As for Domino's phone,
it's probably beyond repair.

256
00:18:49,534 --> 00:18:50,772
But...

257
00:18:50,772 --> 00:18:57,790
I asked if all the videos of Weechana
had been deleted.

258
00:18:58,676 --> 00:19:00,798
Not yet, ma'am.

259
00:19:00,798 --> 00:19:02,713
The videos are still in the iCloud account.

260
00:19:02,713 --> 00:19:04,830
What is iCloud?

261
00:19:04,830 --> 00:19:09,054
ICloud stores photos, videos,
and other data in the cloud,

262
00:19:09,054 --> 00:19:11,260
so you don't need the actual device
to access them.

263
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:13,425
If we know the account and password,

264
00:19:13,425 --> 00:19:16,833
we can access everything
that's stored there, ma'am.

265
00:19:16,833 --> 00:19:19,190
Will it stay there forever?

266
00:19:19,190 --> 00:19:21,094
That's right.

267
00:19:22,940 --> 00:19:26,929
Is it possible that Eva knows?

268
00:19:26,929 --> 00:19:28,784
It is possible, ma'am.

269
00:19:34,766 --> 00:19:36,847
You made a mistake this time.

270
00:19:36,847 --> 00:19:40,386
Please give me another chance.

271
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:44,694
One thing's for sure.

272
00:19:44,694 --> 00:19:47,614
Domino will never wake up again.

273
00:19:48,295 --> 00:19:51,481
If we can't keep Eva under control,

274
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:55,374
we won't be able to keep Weechana's secret
hidden either.

275
00:19:56,057 --> 00:19:58,564
Deal with Domino.

276
00:19:58,564 --> 00:20:00,894
Make sure no one sees you.

277
00:20:01,534 --> 00:20:07,055
As for Eva, let me think about
how to deal with her.

278
00:20:08,697 --> 00:20:10,574
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

279
00:20:11,508 --> 00:20:13,870
Boat, how is Domino?

280
00:20:13,870 --> 00:20:16,644
What did the doctor say? Can we see her now?

281
00:20:16,644 --> 00:20:18,425
She's still in the emergency room.

282
00:20:18,425 --> 00:20:19,966
She has a brain hemorrhage,

283
00:20:19,966 --> 00:20:22,854
both legs are broken,
and she has a fractured arm.

284
00:20:23,540 --> 00:20:26,702
But the doctor says there's still hope.

285
00:20:26,702 --> 00:20:28,681
She didn't hit the ground directly.

286
00:20:28,681 --> 00:20:33,244
She landed on a fabric awning first,
which cushioned the impact.

287
00:20:33,244 --> 00:20:37,694
The doctor says that if she wakes up,
she has a good chance of surviving.

288
00:20:43,537 --> 00:20:46,545
Don't worry. She has to be okay.

289
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:15,833
There are a lot of things I have to do.

290
00:21:15,833 --> 00:21:17,894
Some of them are for my dad,

291
00:21:17,894 --> 00:21:20,095
and sometimes I have to do things
for Weechana.

292
00:21:20,095 --> 00:21:23,294
I was put in the position of
covering up my family's scandals.

293
00:21:25,939 --> 00:21:29,993
That day, I had to create a scene

294
00:21:29,993 --> 00:21:32,654
to distract everyone's attention
at the party.

295
00:21:34,041 --> 00:21:37,540
Distract from what?
Was it really that serious?

296
00:21:41,620 --> 00:21:44,420
The less you know, the better, Pie.

297
00:21:44,420 --> 00:21:46,606
No, I need to know.

298
00:21:46,606 --> 00:21:48,484
Are we still in a relationship?

299
00:21:48,484 --> 00:21:52,094
If we're still together,
then you need to explain all this to me.

300
00:21:52,756 --> 00:21:55,374
Why? Was it really that serious?

301
00:22:01,385 --> 00:22:05,748
That day, Weechana was in the room
with the reporter,

302
00:22:05,748 --> 00:22:07,734
who was later found dead.

303
00:22:08,516 --> 00:22:09,899
What?

304
00:22:11,434 --> 00:22:13,454
You mean Weechana...

305
00:22:14,817 --> 00:22:19,148
I've had to lie to you about a lot of things.

306
00:22:19,148 --> 00:22:21,054
I only did it
because I was worried about you.

307
00:22:22,209 --> 00:22:25,744
That's why I kept telling you
that we shouldn't get too serious.

308
00:22:26,620 --> 00:22:30,934
I don't know if I'd be able
to keep you safe...

309
00:22:32,012 --> 00:22:34,734
if you really became a part of my family.

310
00:22:36,481 --> 00:22:38,416
And you're fine with that?

311
00:22:41,025 --> 00:22:44,796
Baby, We could just move overseas together.

312
00:22:44,796 --> 00:22:46,597
Pie.

313
00:22:49,782 --> 00:22:51,834
I want us to break up.

314
00:22:54,756 --> 00:22:57,134
You'll be safer that way.

315
00:22:58,217 --> 00:23:01,454
In the long run, you might even be happier.

316
00:23:02,092 --> 00:23:05,158
I told you about the reporter

317
00:23:05,158 --> 00:23:09,014
because I didn't want you to remember me
as someone who cheated on you.

318
00:23:12,030 --> 00:23:14,574
Please... stay away from my family.

319
00:23:38,750 --> 00:23:41,374
You're not going to the party meeting today?

320
00:23:42,945 --> 00:23:44,746
Domino fell from the building.

321
00:23:47,734 --> 00:23:49,974
It'll probably be all over the news soon.

322
00:23:54,478 --> 00:23:57,094
Does anyone in this house know about this?

323
00:23:59,161 --> 00:24:00,833
Who did it?

324
00:24:14,859 --> 00:24:16,834
Do you think this was intentional?

325
00:24:20,801 --> 00:24:23,286
What if Weechana's involved in this?

326
00:24:23,286 --> 00:24:24,736
Come on!

327
00:24:25,841 --> 00:24:27,436
No way!

328
00:24:27,436 --> 00:24:29,718
He doesn't seem like a good person, but...

329
00:24:29,718 --> 00:24:32,454
it's his campaign day.

330
00:24:32,454 --> 00:24:34,913
Why would he do something like this?

331
00:24:34,913 --> 00:24:36,854
Who did it?

332
00:24:39,724 --> 00:24:41,694
Or maybe something happened,

333
00:24:42,454 --> 00:24:44,774
and they had to get rid of Domino right away.

334
00:24:44,774 --> 00:24:46,854
Did you know about this?

335
00:24:49,142 --> 00:24:51,942
Do you know

336
00:24:51,942 --> 00:24:55,164
that someone saw you and Weechana
dealing with the reporter that day?

337
00:24:55,164 --> 00:24:57,366
And the reason
Weechana never told you about it

338
00:24:57,366 --> 00:25:02,134
is because the witnesses were Eva and Domino.

339
00:25:02,134 --> 00:25:04,854
I'm taking care of it.

340
00:25:07,137 --> 00:25:09,686
Taking care of what?
You can't handle anything.

341
00:25:09,686 --> 00:25:11,308
The body surfaced.

342
00:25:11,308 --> 00:25:13,868
I had to hear about this from a maid.

343
00:25:13,868 --> 00:25:16,257
Not one of you had the decency
to tell me what happened.

344
00:25:16,257 --> 00:25:18,858
But it didn't have to happen today.

345
00:25:20,161 --> 00:25:23,654
Were you going to let her expose you
after you are elected to Parliament?

346
00:25:25,233 --> 00:25:29,745
Mom, it didn't have to end this way.

347
00:25:29,745 --> 00:25:32,017
This is a big deal.

348
00:25:32,017 --> 00:25:34,105
Why didn't you talk to us first?

349
00:25:34,105 --> 00:25:36,834
And did either of you bother to ask me?

350
00:25:40,985 --> 00:25:43,188
You can leak it to the press,

351
00:25:43,188 --> 00:25:45,121
by saying that the rival parties
are behind it.

352
00:25:45,121 --> 00:25:49,046
Smear campaigns during an election
are nothing unusual.

353
00:25:49,046 --> 00:25:52,934
But this is too big to cover up
with another story.

354
00:25:53,894 --> 00:25:58,004
If anything happens to Domino,
Eva won't help me campaign anymore.

355
00:25:58,004 --> 00:26:00,692
She'll go. Trust me.
I've already talked to her.

356
00:26:00,692 --> 00:26:02,334
What?

357
00:26:02,334 --> 00:26:04,654
You've crossed the line.

358
00:26:09,300 --> 00:26:11,101
Mom, please stop.

359
00:26:14,238 --> 00:26:16,174
Weechana's right.

360
00:26:18,078 --> 00:26:20,694
These days,
we can't cover up one story with another.

361
00:26:23,406 --> 00:26:27,620
If you're sure there's no evidence
linking us to this,

362
00:26:27,620 --> 00:26:29,621
then there's no reason to panic.

363
00:26:31,356 --> 00:26:34,040
I'll take care of the police.

364
00:26:34,040 --> 00:26:36,016
We'll close the case as a suicide
caused by depression,

365
00:26:36,016 --> 00:26:38,184
or maybe say she was drowning in debt.

366
00:26:38,886 --> 00:26:41,134
Eva won't let this go.

367
00:26:44,529 --> 00:26:46,694
If she won't accept it,

368
00:26:46,694 --> 00:26:48,495
then make her accept it.

369
00:26:51,774 --> 00:26:54,054
And if she still won't,

370
00:26:54,841 --> 00:26:56,934
then make sure this stays quiet.

371
00:26:56,934 --> 00:26:58,378
Dad, come on.

372
00:27:01,017 --> 00:27:03,422
You can't do this to Eva.

373
00:27:04,593 --> 00:27:06,817
Then there's only one way.

374
00:27:06,817 --> 00:27:10,434
We need to make her a part of this family
as soon as possible.

375
00:27:12,174 --> 00:27:13,975
What do you mean?

376
00:27:15,265 --> 00:27:17,100
Marry her.

377
00:27:17,100 --> 00:27:19,590
Bring her into this family.

378
00:27:19,590 --> 00:27:22,694
Make sure she's one of us.

379
00:27:27,473 --> 00:27:29,274
That's a great idea.

380
00:27:30,652 --> 00:27:34,294
That'll be a big enough story
to overshadow the Domino story.

381
00:27:36,961 --> 00:27:38,894
You've never approved of our relationship.

382
00:27:42,070 --> 00:27:44,106
You don't like her.

383
00:27:44,106 --> 00:27:48,708
At this point,
it doesn't matter whether I like her or not.

384
00:27:48,708 --> 00:27:50,857
It's your call, Weechana.

385
00:27:50,857 --> 00:27:52,646
Do you want this to go away,

386
00:27:52,646 --> 00:27:55,345
or do you want Eva
to become part of this family,

387
00:27:55,345 --> 00:27:57,984
just like you've always wanted?

388
00:28:01,612 --> 00:28:05,214
Release a statement
saying Eva is no longer campaigning with us.

389
00:28:06,833 --> 00:28:09,984
Because we're respecting her privacy.

390
00:28:12,289 --> 00:28:14,834
Focus on the campaign for now.

391
00:28:16,180 --> 00:28:18,057
When the time is right, propose to her,

392
00:28:18,057 --> 00:28:20,254
and bring her into the family
as soon as possible.

393
00:28:25,829 --> 00:28:28,190
How is she?

394
00:28:28,190 --> 00:28:30,142
Domino has made it
through the critical stage,

395
00:28:30,142 --> 00:28:31,241
but she's still unconscious.

396
00:28:31,241 --> 00:28:34,214
We'll have to keep a close eye on her.

397
00:28:34,214 --> 00:28:36,494
Can I see her?

398
00:28:36,494 --> 00:28:38,014
You can wait outside the room,

399
00:28:38,014 --> 00:28:40,670
because she has to remain
in an isolation room.

400
00:28:40,670 --> 00:28:42,471
Please follow me.

401
00:29:03,260 --> 00:29:04,974
Domino!

402
00:29:04,974 --> 00:29:08,214
Hey! You have to be okay.

403
00:29:15,617 --> 00:29:17,990
Domino! What is happening?

404
00:29:17,990 --> 00:29:19,510
Domino!

405
00:29:19,510 --> 00:29:22,908
Domino! You have to be okay.

406
00:29:22,908 --> 00:29:24,784
Domino!

407
00:29:24,784 --> 00:29:28,294
You have to be fine! Come on!

408
00:29:29,534 --> 00:29:32,084
- Domino!
- 200 joules.

409
00:29:32,084 --> 00:29:33,706
Clear!

410
00:29:37,300 --> 00:29:39,614
The patient has no vital signs.

411
00:29:43,534 --> 00:29:47,134
Time of death: 1:50 PM.

412
00:30:49,980 --> 00:30:51,928
I will ask the hospital

413
00:30:51,928 --> 00:30:55,254
to expedite the investigation
into the cause of death.

414
00:30:55,254 --> 00:30:57,374
According to the nurse,

415
00:30:57,374 --> 00:31:01,001
she was already out of critical condition
and was doing quite well.

416
00:31:01,001 --> 00:31:02,238
Okay.

417
00:31:02,238 --> 00:31:04,940
Please look into it as soon as possible.

418
00:31:04,940 --> 00:31:06,741
And...

419
00:31:07,798 --> 00:31:10,273
I'm going to request an autopsy.

420
00:31:10,273 --> 00:31:11,593
Hey.

421
00:31:17,281 --> 00:31:21,164
If you confirm that she should have survived,

422
00:31:21,164 --> 00:31:25,921
we'll file a police report,
because we believe her death was suspicious.

423
00:31:25,921 --> 00:31:27,286
I agree with that.

424
00:31:27,286 --> 00:31:32,597
Then I'll have someone assist you
with the paperwork.

425
00:31:33,350 --> 00:31:34,763
Got it.

426
00:31:40,812 --> 00:31:42,582
Drink some water.

427
00:31:42,582 --> 00:31:44,383
Your body needs it.

428
00:31:47,249 --> 00:31:48,889
Thank you.

429
00:31:56,208 --> 00:32:00,800
I know you're in shock and grieving
right now,

430
00:32:02,057 --> 00:32:05,630
but I need you to stay calm and listen to me.

431
00:32:07,604 --> 00:32:09,405
Can you do that?

432
00:32:15,688 --> 00:32:17,302
Okay.

433
00:32:17,302 --> 00:32:20,234
Then I need you to tell me
what really happened.

434
00:32:20,945 --> 00:32:25,151
I need to know the truth
so I can keep you safe.

435
00:32:25,953 --> 00:32:27,453
Okay?

436
00:32:34,737 --> 00:32:37,281
Do you really think Domino took her own life?

437
00:32:42,272 --> 00:32:44,718
I'm sure she was murdered.

438
00:32:50,596 --> 00:32:52,397
Domino and I...

439
00:32:54,276 --> 00:32:57,734
We saw Weechana beat a reporter to death.

440
00:33:01,446 --> 00:33:03,454
We also saw...

441
00:33:04,630 --> 00:33:07,180
photos of him with Ginny.

442
00:33:11,054 --> 00:33:13,294
And Domino had a video

443
00:33:13,294 --> 00:33:17,034
of Weechana threatening me
after we had an argument at the gym.

444
00:33:20,598 --> 00:33:23,334
I think she was murdered.

445
00:33:26,342 --> 00:33:29,345
Can you take me to the police?

446
00:33:33,926 --> 00:33:36,614
I'm ready to tell them everything.

447
00:33:37,473 --> 00:33:39,414
I have evidence.

448
00:33:43,173 --> 00:33:44,670
Sure.

449
00:33:46,054 --> 00:33:48,334
But I only trust that one officer.

450
00:33:50,601 --> 00:33:52,295
Who are you talking about?

451
00:33:53,097 --> 00:33:55,337
Police Captain Ekachai.

452
00:33:55,337 --> 00:33:58,454
He was the first officer
who investigated Ginny's case.

453
00:33:58,454 --> 00:34:00,022
Do you remember him?

454
00:34:02,574 --> 00:34:04,375
Sure, I do.

455
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:07,614
Why him?

456
00:34:08,929 --> 00:34:10,702
He asked to speak with me in private

457
00:34:10,702 --> 00:34:12,766
and gave me his business card the other day.

458
00:34:12,766 --> 00:34:14,414
This is my card.

459
00:34:14,414 --> 00:34:16,286
I am working on Ginny's case.

460
00:34:16,286 --> 00:34:18,734
If you happen to come across any leads,
please let me know.

461
00:34:18,734 --> 00:34:19,881
Sure, I will.

462
00:34:19,881 --> 00:34:23,574
<i>He told me he was keeping a close eye
on Weechana.</i>

463
00:34:23,574 --> 00:34:26,854
<i>If anything comes to mind
that you think might help, let him know.</i>

464
00:34:40,684 --> 00:34:42,982
<i>Hello, this is Ekachai.</i>

465
00:34:42,982 --> 00:34:44,783
Hello.

466
00:34:46,294 --> 00:34:48,095
This is Eva.

467
00:34:49,593 --> 00:34:53,139
My manager has just passed away.

468
00:34:53,139 --> 00:34:55,939
I'm at the hospital right now.

469
00:34:55,939 --> 00:34:59,534
I believe she was murdered,

470
00:35:00,649 --> 00:35:03,234
and I think Weechana is involved.

471
00:35:03,865 --> 00:35:05,734
I'd like to meet with you.

472
00:35:13,985 --> 00:35:16,284
Where are you going to stay tonight?

473
00:35:16,284 --> 00:35:18,934
The police probably
won't let you back into the scene yet.

474
00:35:20,174 --> 00:35:22,643
I totally forgot about that.

475
00:35:22,643 --> 00:35:26,441
In that case, if you don't mind,

476
00:35:26,441 --> 00:35:28,153
you can stay at our place tonight.

477
00:35:28,153 --> 00:35:29,954
We will...

478
00:35:32,612 --> 00:35:34,734
It's okay.

479
00:35:34,734 --> 00:35:36,697
Thanks for the offer.

480
00:35:36,697 --> 00:35:40,241
I think I'll stay with my aunt.
I'm worried about her too.

481
00:35:40,241 --> 00:35:41,601
That's probably for the best.

482
00:35:41,601 --> 00:35:43,446
We can give you a ride.

483
00:35:43,446 --> 00:35:47,745
Well... Thank you both so much.

484
00:35:47,745 --> 00:35:50,214
I don't know what I would've done
without you today.

485
00:35:51,281 --> 00:35:53,122
You're welcome.

486
00:36:03,414 --> 00:36:05,894
We're here. Thank you.

487
00:36:15,601 --> 00:36:17,201
Go inside.

488
00:36:17,201 --> 00:36:20,667
We'll wait until you get in safely,
then we'll leave.

489
00:36:27,406 --> 00:36:31,659
Look, we can stay with you if you'd like.

490
00:36:31,659 --> 00:36:34,342
We don't mind staying here with you.
Just say the word.

491
00:36:34,342 --> 00:36:35,911
That's right.

492
00:36:35,911 --> 00:36:38,769
At least you'll feel safe enough
to get some sleep.

493
00:36:38,769 --> 00:36:41,080
If we leave you and your aunt here alone,

494
00:36:41,080 --> 00:36:44,393
I don't think you'll get any sleep tonight.

495
00:36:44,393 --> 00:36:47,334
Yeah... I don't think
I'll be able to sleep either.

496
00:36:50,966 --> 00:36:53,830
I... I mean like...

497
00:36:53,830 --> 00:36:55,324
You know what I mean.

498
00:36:55,324 --> 00:36:57,846
I... I mean...

499
00:36:57,846 --> 00:36:59,814
We're worried about you.

500
00:37:01,548 --> 00:37:04,054
No, it's okay. I don't want to trouble you.

501
00:37:04,054 --> 00:37:07,614
Besides, the house isn't exactly comfortable
right now.

502
00:37:08,801 --> 00:37:10,636
Don't worry about us.

503
00:37:10,636 --> 00:37:13,134
We're not fussy at all.

504
00:37:13,134 --> 00:37:14,694
Yeah.

505
00:37:14,694 --> 00:37:18,457
Domino asked us to look after you,
and we promised her we would.

506
00:37:19,374 --> 00:37:21,254
Let us do this for her.

507
00:37:24,902 --> 00:37:26,402
Okay.

508
00:37:28,334 --> 00:37:29,847
Should we go?

509
00:37:35,614 --> 00:37:38,294
Hello, Mr. Noppol.

510
00:37:39,174 --> 00:37:43,814
I'm afraid I need to ask for your help again.

511
00:37:44,820 --> 00:37:46,569
<i>Go ahead, Mr. Chaichana.</i>

512
00:37:46,569 --> 00:37:48,942
<i>If there's anything I can do,
I'll help, just like always.</i>

513
00:37:49,734 --> 00:37:51,734
Thank you so much, sir.

514
00:37:56,114 --> 00:37:58,014
Make yourselves at home.

515
00:37:58,014 --> 00:37:59,815
Thank you.

516
00:38:05,516 --> 00:38:06,881
Make yourselves at home.

517
00:38:06,881 --> 00:38:09,761
If you need anything, just let me know.

518
00:38:09,761 --> 00:38:11,369
